# Read one container of your own Azure storage account.
# - The account is the host, <account>.blob.core.windows.net, and every container in the account
#   is a first path segment. Allowing the whole host would allow every public container of the
#   account, so the tree keeps the reach to this one container.
# - Azure's rule makes container names lowercase, so the path is written that way.
# - The line grants reads only. The proxy refuses and logs a request outside the tree, or one
#   spelled outside a rule path's canonical form (doc/egress-proxy.md, "The rule file"). The proxy
#   therefore also refuses a blob whose name needs an ASCII character other than a space escaped
#   on the wire.
# - A SAS upload URL still fails here: the proxy refuses a PUT where no line grants it.
# - What travels in an allowed GET's suffix and query is not bounded (SECURITY.md, "Exfiltration
#   through allowed network traffic").
allow https://myaccount.blob.core.windows.net/my-container/ read
